WEBVTT

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:18.640
Do you hear?  Hooves beating

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:30.750
A carriage goes through the gentle hills

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:38.030
Someone comes to pick me up

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:45.980
And takes me

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:49.950
To the avenue with white flowers

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:58.070
To the home of wind

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.450
He takes me

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.900
I'm sure

00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:31.940
Three weeks have passed
since Anne started school.

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:33.650
Good morning!

00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:36.580
Three weeks have passed
since Anne started school.

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:43.680
After Mr. Phillips humiliated her,
she worked very hard in her lessons.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:51.780
She was like the parched ground,
absorbing the rain water greedy and quickly.

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:54.930
I guess Gilbert Blythe will be in school today.

00:01:56.550 --> 00:02:00.680
Gil's been visiting his cousins over
in New Brunswick all summer

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:04.160
and he only came home Saturday night.

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:05.250
Gil?

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:07.780
Yes! Gilbert Blythe!

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:10.040
He's awfully handsome, Anne!

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:15.390
And he teases the girls something terrible.
He just torments our lives out.

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:25.160
Gilbert Blythe? Isn't his name that's written
up on the porch wall with Julia Bell's

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:27.690
and a big 'Take Notice' over them?

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:33.670
Yes. But I'm sure he doesn't like
Julia Bell so very much.

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:39.620
Because I've heard him say he studied the
multiplication table by her freckles.

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:45.670
Oh, don't speak about freckles to me.
It isn't delicate when I've got so many.

00:02:46.690 --> 00:02:49.490
But I do think that writing take-notices
up on the wall about

00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:52.330
the boys and girls is the silliest thing ever.

00:02:52.910 --> 00:02:57.870
I should just like to see anybody dare to
write my name up with a boy's.

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:00.930
Not, of course, that anybody would.

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:04.160
Nonsense! It's only meant as a joke.

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:08.260
And don't you be too sure your
name won't ever be written up.

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:11.010
Charlie Sloane is dead gone on you.

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:16.080
He told his mother...
His MOTHER, mind you...

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:19.680
That you were the smartest girl in school.

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:22.750
That's better than being good looking.

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:27.550
No, it isn't!
I'd rather be pretty than clever.

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:32.720
And I hate Charlie Sloane, I can't
bear a boy with goggle eyes.

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:40.030
But, you won't find it so easy to
keep head of your class, Anne.

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:42.370
You'll have Gilbert in your class now.

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:46.760
He's only in the fourth book
although he's nearly fourteen.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:50.490
Four years ago his father was
sick and had to go to Alberta,

00:03:50.490 --> 00:03:52.150
and Gilbert went with him.

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:55.630
He hardly came to school during three years.

00:03:55.970 --> 00:03:58.000
But Gil is so smart!

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:05.800
So you won't find it so easy to
keep head after this, Anne.

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:08.060
I'm glad!

00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:15.980
I couldn't really feel proud of keeping head
of little boys and girls of just nine or ten.

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:21.410
Hi!

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:24.380
Wait a minute!

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:25.110
Yes.

00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:33.180
Here!

00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:34.600
Gilbert!

00:04:34.690 --> 00:04:36.070
Uncle, I'm back!

00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:37.320
I'm going to school!

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:41.820
Take good care of your father!

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:44.650
Yes, of course!
You don't need to tell me!

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:56.020
Watch!

00:05:02.510 --> 00:05:03.330
Got it.

00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:11.820
Good morning, Anne, Dianna.

00:05:12.130 --> 00:05:13.260
Good morning, Charlie!

00:05:13.990 --> 00:05:14.930
Good morning.

00:05:20.970 --> 00:05:22.560
Well, I'm going first.

00:05:25.070 --> 00:05:25.940
Gilbert!

00:05:25.940 --> 00:05:27.050
Welcome back!

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:27.710
You're so late!

00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:28.930
Gilbert, good morning!

00:05:29.410 --> 00:05:30.180
Let's go.

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:30.660
Yes.

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:33.400
Good morning!

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:58.280
That's Gilbert Blythe sitting right
across the aisle from you.

00:05:59.240 --> 00:06:01.720
Look at him and see if he isn't handsome.

00:06:23.050 --> 00:06:24.440
Mr. Phillips, I'm done!

00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:27.950
What happened?

00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:32.170
Silence. Ruby, pay attention!

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:36.460
Silence!

00:06:57.720 --> 00:07:00.560
I think your Gilbert Blythe is handsome,

00:07:00.950 --> 00:07:02.930
but he's very bold.

00:07:03.630 --> 00:07:06.870
It isn't good manners to wink at a strange girl.

00:07:06.870 --> 00:07:08.010
Wink?

00:07:16.090 --> 00:07:16.850
Got it!

00:07:17.530 --> 00:07:19.580
Wait! What are you doing?

00:09:39.330 --> 00:09:40.810
Carrots! Carrots!

00:09:46.210 --> 00:09:48.500
You mean, hateful boy!

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:51.390
How dare you!

00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:14.900
Anne Shirley, what does this mean?

00:10:20.310 --> 00:10:23.360
It was my fault Mr. Phillips.
I teased her.

00:10:25.490 --> 00:10:27.510
That doesn't matter!

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:35.530
I am sorry to see a pupil of mine displaying
such a temper and such a vindictive spirit.

00:10:36.040 --> 00:10:38.320
Anne Shirley, look at me!

00:10:40.600 --> 00:10:46.420
Anne, go and stand in front of the
blackboard for the rest of the afternoon.

00:11:03.990 --> 00:11:06.360
Josie Pye, read it, please.

00:11:06.400 --> 00:11:07.100
Yes.

00:11:07.440 --> 00:11:10.180
Ann Shirley has a very bad temper.

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:14.650
Ann Shirley must learn to control her temper.

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:17.320
Yes, that's right!

00:11:36.360 --> 00:11:37.250
Anne Shirley!

00:11:41.440 --> 00:11:42.250
Anne!

00:11:46.120 --> 00:11:48.580
I'm awfully sorry I made fun of your hair.

00:11:49.110 --> 00:11:50.700
Honest, I am.

00:11:53.230 --> 00:11:56.320
Anne, don't be mad for keeps, now.

00:12:02.070 --> 00:12:02.920
Anne!

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:14.980
Anne, how could you?

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:18.520
I shall never forgive Gilbert Blythe!

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:23.770
You mustn't mind Gilbert
making fun of your hair.

00:12:24.880 --> 00:12:27.290
Why, he makes fun of all the girls.

00:12:27.910 --> 00:12:31.640
He laughs at mine because it's so black.

00:12:32.200 --> 00:12:34.900
He's called me a crow a dozen times.

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:40.150
And I never heard him apologize
for anything before, either.

00:12:40.700 --> 00:12:44.560
There's a great deal of difference between
being called a crow and being called carrots.

00:12:45.260 --> 00:12:50.420
Gilbert Blythe has hurt my
feelings EXCRUCIATINGLY, Diana!

00:12:52.400 --> 00:12:55.640
It is possible the matter might have blown over

00:12:55.640 --> 00:13:00.260
without more excruciation
if nothing else had happened.

00:13:00.260 --> 00:13:06.210
But when things begin to
happen they are apt to keep on.

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:11.940
In the next morning,

00:13:11.940 --> 00:13:17.260
all the boys and some of the girls went
to Mr. Bell's spruce grove as usual,

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:20.110
fully intending to stay only long
enough to pick gum.

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:28.340
And,

00:13:28.340 --> 00:13:30.860
Anne, who had not been picking gum at all,

00:13:30.860 --> 00:13:35.170
was wandering happily in the far end of the
grove, singing softly to herself.

00:13:37.860 --> 00:13:39.590
He's here! He's coming!

00:13:41.100 --> 00:13:42.040
Hurry!

00:13:43.800 --> 00:13:44.400
Wait for me!

00:14:17.640 --> 00:14:23.530
Have you forgotten that I expected you to
wait in your seat before I return?

00:14:23.610 --> 00:14:25.240
What a disappointment!

00:14:26.380 --> 00:14:28.050
And Anne Shirley...

00:14:29.370 --> 00:14:33.120
What's that horrible thing in your hair?
Take that off!

00:14:33.460 --> 00:14:38.810
And since you seem to be so
fond of the boys company,

00:14:39.310 --> 00:14:43.060
we shall indulge your taste for it this afternoon.

00:14:44.750 --> 00:14:49.660
Now go and sit with Gilbert Blythe.

00:14:54.720 --> 00:14:55.890
That's horrible!

00:15:02.410 --> 00:15:05.450
Did you hear what I said, Anne?

00:15:06.010 --> 00:15:07.470
Yes, sir.

00:15:07.790 --> 00:15:10.190
But I didn't suppose you really meant it.

00:15:10.190 --> 00:15:12.510
I assure you I did.

00:15:12.770 --> 00:15:15.690
Obey me at once, Anne!

00:15:20.550 --> 00:15:21.270
Anne...

00:15:36.060 --> 00:15:37.550
How deserving.

00:15:44.690 --> 00:15:45.880
Well...

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:49.890
Please gather your thoughts
and prepare for lessons.

00:15:50.040 --> 00:15:52.960
History for fourth grade.
Come forward.

00:15:53.100 --> 00:15:55.020
Yes.

00:16:42.360 --> 00:16:44.540
Please everyone continue
working hard tomorrow.

00:16:53.080 --> 00:16:56.160
Please, don't be angry with me anymore?

00:17:13.780 --> 00:17:14.750
What's wrong?

00:17:14.750 --> 00:17:14.840
Anne?
What's wrong?

00:17:14.840 --> 00:17:15.500
Anne?

00:17:27.410 --> 00:17:29.520
What are you taking all those things home for?

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:31.770
I am not coming back to school any more!

00:17:38.040 --> 00:17:41.430
But, will Marilla let you stay home?

00:17:41.790 --> 00:17:43.260
She'll have to.

00:17:43.640 --> 00:17:45.280
I'll NEVER go to school again.

00:17:45.280 --> 00:17:48.160
You're mean, Anne!
What shall I do?

00:17:48.390 --> 00:17:53.060
Mr. Phillips will make me sit
with that horrid Gertie Pye.

00:17:53.200 --> 00:17:54.920
Do come back, Anne.

00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:58.500
I'd do almost anything in the world for you.

00:17:58.590 --> 00:18:02.810
I'd let myself be torn limb from limb
if it would do you any good.

00:18:02.960 --> 00:18:04.820
But I can't do this.

00:18:07.470 --> 00:18:12.130
So please don't ask it.
You harrow up my very soul.

00:18:13.160 --> 00:18:17.450
But just think of all the fun you will miss.

00:18:18.020 --> 00:18:22.510
We're playing ball next week and you've
never played ball before, did you?

00:18:22.510 --> 00:18:24.150
It's tremendously exciting.

00:18:24.150 --> 00:18:26.130
We're going to learn a new song.

00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:31.760
Jane  is going to bring a new Pansy book
and we're all going to read it out loud.

00:18:31.930 --> 00:18:34.780
And you are so fond of
reading out loud, Anne.

00:19:09.880 --> 00:19:10.630
Nonsense.

00:19:10.900 --> 00:19:12.580
It isn't nonsense at all.

00:19:12.580 --> 00:19:15.860
Don't you understand, Marilla?
I've been insulted.

00:19:15.970 --> 00:19:18.000
Insulted? Fiddlesticks!

00:19:18.190 --> 00:19:20.740
You'll go to school tomorrow as usual.

00:19:20.740 --> 00:19:21.610
Oh, no.

00:19:22.700 --> 00:19:25.080
I'm not going back, Marilla.

00:19:25.080 --> 00:19:26.810
I'll learn my lessons at home,

00:19:26.810 --> 00:19:31.190
and I'll be as good as I can be and hold my
tongue all the time if it's possible at all.

00:19:31.200 --> 00:19:34.540
But I will not go back to
school, I assure you.

00:19:40.430 --> 00:19:40.880
Anne...

00:19:40.880 --> 00:19:42.300
Please don't say anymore!

00:19:49.010 --> 00:19:53.310
Mr. Phillips has been carrying
matters with a rather high hand.

00:19:56.690 --> 00:19:59.000
Now, what shall I do?

00:19:59.720 --> 00:20:05.020
Marilla didn't continue bickering
with Anne at her determination,

00:20:05.020 --> 00:20:07.710
and chose to discuss it with Mrs. Rachel Lynde.

00:20:07.710 --> 00:20:13.450
She's sent ten children to school and
she ought to know something about it.

00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:17.590
I suppose you know what I've come about,
isn't that right Rachel?

00:20:19.040 --> 00:20:23.380
And if you want my opinion about it,
I will give it to you Marilla.

00:20:23.800 --> 00:20:28.670
From what I heard from Tillie, I think
Mr. Phillips was in the wrong this time.

00:20:29.660 --> 00:20:32.350
I  think so too.

00:20:32.780 --> 00:20:36.170
Of course, it doesn't do
to say so to the children.

00:20:36.340 --> 00:20:40.440
He did right to punish her yesterday
for giving way to temper.

00:20:40.720 --> 00:20:43.140
But today it was different.

00:20:43.430 --> 00:20:48.670
The others who were late
should have been punished as well.

00:20:48.880 --> 00:20:55.380
And I don't believe in making the
girls sit with the boys for punishment.

00:20:55.380 --> 00:20:57.270
It isn't modest.

00:20:58.430 --> 00:20:59.770
I think so too.

00:20:59.770 --> 00:21:01.670
Tillie was real indignant.

00:21:01.680 --> 00:21:07.440
She took Anne's part right through
and said all the scholars did too.

00:21:07.820 --> 00:21:16.060
Anne seems real popular among them.
I never thought she'd take with them so well.

00:21:17.410 --> 00:21:22.160
I'd just humor her a little
at first, that's what I'd do.

00:21:23.190 --> 00:21:27.440
Then Rachel, you really think
I'd better let her stay home!

00:21:27.440 --> 00:21:34.940
Yes. That is, I wouldn't say school to
her again until she said it herself.

00:21:35.330 --> 00:21:42.140
She'll cool off in a week or so and be ready
enough to go back of her own accord.

00:21:42.460 --> 00:21:48.760
If you were to make her go back now, dear
knows what tantrum she'd take next.

00:21:48.760 --> 00:21:53.120
Mr. Phillips isn't any good at all as a teacher!

00:21:53.120 --> 00:21:58.320
The order he keeps is scandalous, that's
what, and he neglects the young fry

00:21:58.320 --> 00:22:03.270
and puts all his time on those big scholars
he's getting ready for Queen's.

00:22:17.200 --> 00:22:19.200
I'm sorry, Diana!

00:22:28.460 --> 00:22:29.720
Anne, I'm coming in!

00:22:33.630 --> 00:22:35.320
Is this about school, Marilla?

00:22:35.510 --> 00:22:37.940
Of course. What else could it be?

00:22:37.940 --> 00:22:40.700
No matter what, I'm determined.

00:22:40.890 --> 00:22:42.580
I won't go back to school.

00:22:43.130 --> 00:22:46.630
I respect your opinion this time, Anne.

00:22:48.690 --> 00:22:53.710
If you don't want to go back to school,
I don't think I'll help any by worrying.

00:22:53.710 --> 00:22:56.060
Then, Marilla...

00:22:59.460 --> 00:23:02.680
You can stay at home
If you don't want to go.

00:23:02.840 --> 00:23:06.520
Oh, Marilla, you understood my feelings!

00:23:09.810 --> 00:23:12.880
My, my. I'm not done yet, Anne.

00:23:13.170 --> 00:23:16.790
Just as you said, if you are not to go
to school, you have to study at home.

00:23:17.120 --> 00:23:18.440
That's what you said.

00:23:21.800 --> 00:23:26.160
And you will have to study and
help the housework at the same time.

00:23:26.550 --> 00:23:29.190
You are not a child anymore.

00:23:30.120 --> 00:23:32.320
First I'll teach you cooking.

00:23:32.370 --> 00:23:33.500
Marilla...

00:23:34.170 --> 00:23:36.230
I'll do my very best.

00:23:37.400 --> 00:23:39.010
Thank you, Marilla.

00:23:44.620 --> 00:23:48.280
Well now, you don't have
to be so worried, Marilla.

00:23:48.890 --> 00:23:52.130
Of course you wouldn't
think this to be a problem.

00:23:52.550 --> 00:23:58.130
But I wonder if Rachel is right, and if
that girl will want return to school one day.

00:23:58.660 --> 00:24:00.710
When I think of this...

00:24:01.230 --> 00:24:04.750
Well now, don't you worry.

00:24:17.750 --> 00:24:24.770
Anne spends her first autumn in Green
Gables after being away from school.

00:24:25.070 --> 00:24:27.640
Next of Anne of Green Gables:

00:24:27.640 --> 00:24:29.460
The Coming of Autumn

00:24:29.470 --> 00:24:30.470
Please watch.
